invariant: INV-14
file: srv.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_host
reason: the server init calls of a host object stop asking for the
  caller's description of its CPU, so ch_srv_record_init takes a
  configuration that never set ch_cfg.cpu. ch_srv_check keeps its own
  rule, so only the init rows notice: test/tcp_nonblocking_loop_cpu.h
  requires CH_EINVAL and a failed session for 0.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    // The caller's description of its CPU (cpu_cfg.h), before any rule
    // that reads it.
    if (!cpu_bits_ok(cfg)) {
        return 0;
    }
#endif
--- new
